  "latest_work": "Network/name/descending per-slot stack-count sorting is implemented and scoped stock-client accepted on both legacy ports. The client exposed a 1.6.4 saved-tool binding bug: normalize only the NBT root transport name on a copy while preserving the full binding payload and all authorization checks. 1.12.2 passed 168 native cases; the repaired 1.6.4 passed 170; main passed 192. All 24 exact native tracks qualify their recorded source/JAR hashes across the documented runs. Both stock clients passed real mouse sort/order/replay/transfer/paging, four GUI scales and display privacy; all 16 captures were reviewed and preserved. Prior failed compile/client runs remain recorded. Search/grouping, editor/multipart and broader acceptance stay open; no RC is cleared or published.",
